## Role
You are a frontend developer working on a Next.js application called SpecBuilder.
Focus on UI implementation only. Do not suggest changes to backend logic or shared schemas.

---

## Project Overview
SpecBuilder is a workflow-based AI tool that converts Minutes of Meeting (MOM)
into structured specification documents.
Target users: Business Analysts (BA) and Project Managers (PM).
Not a chat AI — AI is only called in controlled workflow steps.

---

## Tech Stack
- Framework:     Next.js 16.2 (App Router)
- Language:      TypeScript (strict, no `any`)
- Styling:       Tailwind CSS v4
- UI Library:    HeroUI (@heroui/react) — https://www.heroui.com
- Forms:         react-hook-form + @hookform/resolvers/zod
- Validation:    Zod schemas from @spec-app/schemas ONLY — never write schemas here
- Icons:         lucide-react
- DnD:           @dnd-kit/core + @dnd-kit/sortable (template section reordering)

---

## Next.js 16 Specific Rules
- Turbopack is now the default bundler — do not add --turbopack flags, it runs automatically
- middleware.ts is DEPRECATED — use proxy.ts with exported function named `proxy` instead
- React Compiler is stable — do not manually add useMemo/useCallback unless truly necessary,
  the compiler handles memoization automatically
- `use cache` directive replaces PPR — use this for caching components/functions if needed
- App Router conventions apply — server components by default, `use client` only when needed

---

## Monorepo Context
```
spec-app/
  backend/
  frontend/         ← this app
  mobile/
  packages/
    schemas/        ← shared Zod schemas (@spec-app/schemas)
```
Always import types and schemas from `@spec-app/schemas`.
Never duplicate types that already exist as inferred types from those schemas.

---

## Current Mode: UI DEMO ONLY
- No real API calls — all data comes from mock files in `src/mocks/`
- Mock functions simulate async with 300-500ms delay using `delay()` helper
- All mock functions return `Promise<ApiResponse<T>>`
- Service files exist as shells with `// TODO: replace with real API call`
- Use realistic mock data — no "string", "test", "lorem ipsum"
- API wiring happens after demo

---

## API Response Type
Define once in `src/types/api.types.ts`:
```typescript
export interface ApiResponse<T> {
  status: number;
  message: string;
  data: T;
}
```

---

## App Router Structure
```
src/
  app/
    (auth)/
      login/
        page.tsx
    (dashboard)/
      layout.tsx              ← sidebar layout wrapper
      dashboard/
        page.tsx
      specifications/
        page.tsx
        [id]/
          page.tsx
        create/
          page.tsx
      templates/
        page.tsx
        create/
          page.tsx
        [id]/
          edit/
            page.tsx
  components/
    layout/
      sidebar.tsx
      topbar.tsx
    ui/                       ← shared reusable components
    specs/                    ← spec-specific components
    templates/                ← template-specific components
  mocks/
    auth.mock.ts
    spec.mock.ts
    template.mock.ts
  services/                   ← empty shells, TODO comments only
    auth.service.ts
    spec.service.ts
    template.service.ts
  types/
    api.types.ts
  lib/
    mock-utils.ts
    utils.ts
```

---

## Routing
- `/` → redirect to `/dashboard`
- Auth: hardcoded redirect for demo, no real session check
- Add next-auth after demo — do not wire it now
- All protected pages live under `(dashboard)` route group
- Do NOT use middleware.ts — use proxy.ts if request interception is needed

---

## Design System

### Overall Feel
- Working tool aesthetic — think Linear, Vercel dashboard, not a SaaS marketing page
- Compact density — tighter spacing, less padding than typical marketing designs
- Strong typographic hierarchy
- Functional over decorative — reduce icons and decorative elements

### Layout
- Sidebar: fixed left, 240px wide, dark (`zinc-900`)
- Content area: fills remaining width, light background (`zinc-50`)
- Topbar: inside content area, white bg, border-bottom, 64px tall
- Page content: padded container, 24px padding

### Sidebar Structure
```
Top:
  [SpecBuilder logo + icon]

Navigation:
  - Dashboard         (LayoutDashboard icon)
  - Specifications    (FileText icon)
  - Templates         (Layout icon)

Bottom:
  - Theme toggle
  - User avatar + name
  - Logout button
```

Sidebar item states:
- Inactive: zinc-400 text, transparent bg
- Active:   white text, zinc-800 bg, rounded-md
- Hover:    zinc-700 bg

### Color Palette
- Sidebar bg:        zinc-900
- Sidebar text:      zinc-400 (inactive), white (active)
- Sidebar active:    zinc-800
- Content bg:        zinc-50
- Card bg:           white
- Border:            zinc-200
- Primary:           blue-600
- Danger:            red-500
- Success:           green-600
- Warning:           amber-500
- Processing:        blue-500

### Status Badge Colors
- PROCESSING  → blue badge + animated Loader2 spinner icon
- COMPLETED   → green badge
- REVIEWED    → green badge + CheckCircle icon
- FAILED      → red badge + AlertCircle icon
- EXPORTED    → purple badge + Download icon

---

## Mock Helpers (`src/lib/mock-utils.ts`)
```typescript
export const delay = (ms: number) => new Promise(res => setTimeout(res, ms));

export function mockResponse<T>(data: T, status = 200): ApiResponse<T> {
  return { status, message: 'success', data };
}
```

---

## Mock Data Scale
- 5-6 mock specs with mixed statuses: PROCESSING, COMPLETED, REVIEWED, FAILED, EXPORTED
- 4 mock templates: Standard Template, Mobile App Template, API Template, UI/UX Template
  - Mix of English and Thai — at least 1 Thai template
  - Each with realistic section titles and descriptions
- 1 spec with 3 versions (demo version history tab)
- 1 spec with 3-4 risks (demo ambiguities tab)
  - Each risk must include: priority, type, related section name, title, MOM quote
- Realistic names, dates, content — not placeholder text

---

## Page Specifications

### Login (`/login`)
- Centered card layout, full screen
- SpecBuilder logo + name at top of card
- Email + password fields using react-hook-form + zodResolver
  with LoginSchema from @spec-app/schemas
- "Sign In" button (full width)
- On submit: mock login 500ms delay → redirect to /dashboard
- No register link (admin creates users externally)

---

### Dashboard (`/dashboard`)
Sections top to bottom:

1. Page header
   - Title: "Specification Management"
   - Subtitle: "Transform meeting notes into structured, unambiguous project specifications"
   - "+ Create Specification" button → /specifications/create

2. Stats row — 4 compact stat cards:
   - My Specifications (total count, document icon)
   - Reviewed (count, green check icon)
   - Processing (count, blue spinner icon if > 0)
   - Failed (count, red alert icon if > 0, red text)

3. Workflow steps — compact horizontal stepper (visual only, not clickable):
   - Step 1: Import MOM
   - Step 2: Select Template
   - Step 3: Generate Spec
   - Step 4: Review
   Connected by arrows, numbered circles

4. Recent Activity — last 5 specs as list rows:
   - Document icon + title + template info (muted)
   - Status badge
   - Relative time (e.g. "2 hours ago")
   - Click row → /specifications/[id]

DO NOT include:
- Available Templates section
- "Ready to Create Your First Specification?" hero section
- Getting Started tab

---

### Specifications List (`/specifications`)

- Page header: "Specifications" + subtitle + "+ New Spec" button → /specifications/create
- Search input: "Search by title or template..."
- Filters row: Status dropdown | Language dropdown | Sort By dropdown
- Count: "Showing X of Y specifications"

Each spec row:
- Document icon
- Title (bold) + subtitle: "[Template] • v[N] • [N] sections"
- Language badge
- Status badge (with spinner for PROCESSING)
- Date
- ⋮ menu:
  - View → /specifications/[id]
  - Regenerate (confirmation modal)
  - Mark as Reviewed (only if not already REVIEWED)

PROCESSING behavior:
- Badge shows spinner
- Poll every 4 seconds (mock: useEffect interval)
- On COMPLETED: show toast "✓ [name] is ready to review"
- Clear interval when no longer PROCESSING

Empty state:
- Icon + "No specifications yet"
- "Create your first specification to get started"
- "+ Create Specification" button

---

### Create Specification (`/specifications/create`)
2-step wizard only — NOT 4 steps.

Progress bar: Step 1 → Step 2, checkmark on completed step.

**Step 1 — Meeting Notes:**
- Card title: "Paste Your Meeting Notes"
- Subtitle: "Copy and paste the minutes of meeting (MOM) from your recent discussion."

Two input methods (tabs or toggle):

  Option A — Type/Paste (default tab):
  - Textarea: label "Meeting Notes (MOM)", min 50 characters
  - Info tip: "Tip: Include as much detail as possible about requirements,
    stakeholders, timelines, and any special considerations."

  Option B — Upload File:
  - Drag and drop area or click to browse
  - Accepted formats: .txt, .docx, .pdf
  - Shows filename + file size after selection
  - Read-only — no text extraction for demo
  - Note: "File will be processed on the server"
  - Backend contract (for future wiring):
    - Text paste  → JSON:           { momContent: string, templateId, language }
    - File upload → multipart/form: { file, templateId, language }

- Button: "Next: Select Template →" (disabled until input is valid)

**Step 2 — Select Template & Language:**
- Card title: "Select Template & Language"
- Template grid (2×2): Standard, Mobile App, API, UI/UX
  - Each card: name, short description, section count
  - Selected state: blue border + blue check badge
- Language:
  - Radio: English / Thai (ไทย)
  - Note: "Changing language later will require generating a new version"
- Buttons: "← Back" | "Generate Specification →"

**On submit:**
- Create mock spec status: PROCESSING
- Redirect immediately to /specifications
- Spec at top of list with PROCESSING badge + spinner
- After 5 seconds: status → COMPLETED
- Toast: "✓ [spec name] is ready to review"

---

### Specification Detail (`/specifications/[id]`)

**Header:**
- "← Back to Specifications"
- Title (large bold) + subtitle (muted)
- Badges: Status + Language + Version (e.g. "v2")
- Right: ⋮ menu + "Export PDF" button (blue)

**⋮ menu:**
- Mark as Reviewed (only if not REVIEWED)
  - Confirmation modal:
    "Marking as reviewed indicates this spec has been checked —
    not that it is final or approved. Continue?"
  - On confirm: update status locally
- Regenerate → opens regenerate confirmation modal

**Regenerate modal:**
- Default: "This will create a new version. Previous versions remain viewable."
- If language changed, add warning:
  "Changing language may affect:
   • Word and terminology choices
   • Content structure
   • Ambiguity detection results"
- Buttons: Cancel | Confirm

**Export PDF:**
- On click: toast "Exporting PDF..."
- After 1 second: toast "PDF exported successfully"
- No actual file generation for demo

**Metadata row (card):**
- Template | Created By | Created Date | Last Modified

**Original MOM — collapsible section** (below metadata, collapsed by default):
- Toggle: "View Original Meeting Notes (MOM)" + ChevronDown icon
- Expands to: scrollable read-only box, monospace font, max-height 200px
- No edit controls

**3 tabs:**

Tab 1 — Specification:
- Section cards in template order
- Each card: "[N]. Section Title" (bold) + content paragraph
- Empty content → italic muted: "Not mentioned in the provided information (MOM)"

Tab 2 — Ambiguities & Risks:
- Summary: "Found X potential ambiguities or risks. Please review and clarify."
- Each risk card (FR-RISK-02):
  - Priority badge: High (red) | Medium (amber) | Low (green)
  - Type badge: e.g. "Ambiguous word", "Unclear scope", "Missing timeline"
  - Related section name (muted, e.g. "→ User Requirements")
  - Risk title (bold)
  - MOM reference quote (italic muted, in quotation marks)
- NO "Mark as Resolved" button
- NO "Add Note" button
- Empty state: green CheckCircle + "No ambiguities or risks detected"

Tab 3 — Versions:
- Title: "Version History"
- Each row:
  - "Version X" + "Current" badge on latest COMPLETED/REVIEWED version
  - Date + short description
  - "View" button
- NO "Restore" button

**Page states:**
- PROCESSING: HeroUI Skeleton + banner "Your specification is being generated..."
- FAILED: red banner "Generation failed. Please try regenerating." + Regenerate button
- COMPLETED / REVIEWED / EXPORTED: full content

---

### Templates List (`/templates`)

- Page header: "Templates" + "+ New Template" button → /templates/create
- Grid (2 columns) of template cards:
  - Template name (bold)
  - Language badge
  - Section count
  - Created date
  - ⋮ menu:
    - Edit → /templates/[id]/edit
    - Delete → confirmation modal "Are you sure? This cannot be undone."
    - On confirm: remove from local state + success toast

Empty state:
- Icon + "No templates yet"
- "Create your first template to get started"
- "+ New Template" button

---

### Create Template (`/templates/create`)
### Edit Template (`/templates/[id]/edit`)
Same component, two modes.

**Header:**
- "← Back to Templates"
- Title: "Create Template" or "Edit Template"

**Fields:**
- Template Name: text input, required
- Language: radio English | Thai (ไทย)
  - DISABLED on edit mode
  - Tooltip: "Language cannot be changed after creation"

**Sections:**
- Each row:
  - GripVertical icon (drag handle, cursor-grab)
  - Section number (auto-calculated, read-only)
  - Title input (required, placeholder "Section title")
  - Description textarea (required, placeholder "Describe what AI should
    extract for this section — used as guidance for AI generation")
  - Trash icon delete button
    - Disabled when only 1 section remains
    - Tooltip: "Template must have at least one section"
- Drag to reorder via @dnd-kit/sortable
- "+ Add Section" button below list

**Actions:**
- "Cancel" → /templates
- "Save Template" → 300ms mock delay → /templates + success toast

**Validation (inline errors on submit):**
- Template name required
- At least 1 section
- Each section: title + description required

---

## Component Rules
- Server components by default
- `'use client'` only for: forms, interactive state, polling, DnD
- Forms: react-hook-form + zodResolver always
- Never write inline Zod schemas — import from @spec-app/schemas
- Never use `any`
- Use `import type` for type-only imports in decorated contexts
- Do NOT manually add useMemo/useCallback — React Compiler handles this

---

## Loading & Empty States
Every data page must handle:
- Loading: HeroUI Skeleton components
- Empty: icon + message + CTA button
- Error: error message + retry/action button

---

## State Management
- Local useState for all UI state
- No global store needed for demo
- Polling: useEffect + setInterval, always clear on unmount or status change
- Toast: HeroUI addToast

---

## What NOT To Do
- Do not write Zod schemas — always import from @spec-app/schemas
- Do not make real API calls — use mock functions only
- Do not add authentication logic — hardcoded redirect for demo
- Do not use pages/ router — App Router only
- Do not use `any` in TypeScript
- Do not use middleware.ts — deprecated in Next.js 16, use proxy.ts
- Do not add --turbopack flag — it runs by default in Next.js 16
- Do not manually add useMemo/useCallback — React Compiler handles memoization
- Do not add "Mark as Resolved" or "Add Note" to risk cards
- Do not add "Restore" button to version history
- Do not use a top navbar — sidebar only
- Do not include Available Templates section on dashboard
- Do not include hero/CTA section on dashboard
- Do not use a 4-step wizard — 2 steps only
- Do not add username field — email only
- Do not generate actual PDF — toast only for demo
- Do not allow language change on template edit mode
- Do not allow deleting the last remaining section of a template
- Do not extract text from uploaded files on frontend — backend handles extraction
